---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "multipotentialite — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>multipotentialite</h1>
    <p>a multipotentialite (coined by emilie wapnick) has many interests and refuses to choose just one. instead of seeing this as a lack of focus, it's a strength: you spot problems others miss because you see across silos, and you get bored when learning plateaus, so you naturally seek depth in one area before moving on.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>embrace your many interests rather than fighting them</li>
      <li>seek depth within each interest before abandoning it</li>
      <li>look for meta-skills (communication, systems thinking) that transfer between interests</li>
      <li>find work or projects that let you use multiple skills (design + writing + code, for example)</li>
      <li>understand your pattern: are you a scanner (wide, shallow), a diver (deep in one, then switch), or a hybrid?</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="care">multipotentialite does not equal procrastinator. real depth requires sticking with something long enough to hit the messy middle.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
